Authentication flow
•	Client POSTs JSON to /api/auth/pin-login with customerNumber and pin (4 chars).
•	Server validates input, looks up Customer by CustomerNumber, then CustomerCredential.
•	Server verifies PIN via PasswordHasher<CustomerCredential>.VerifyHashedPassword.
•	On success:
•	Reset FailedAttemptCount and LockedUntil; set LastSuccessfulLogin.
•	Create CustomerSession with:
•	SessionId = new Guid()
•	TokenHash = SHA256(Base64(tokenBytes)) stored in DB (so raw token not stored)
•	ExpiresOn = UtcNow + 1 hour
•	CreatedOn = UtcNow
•	Return 200 OK with expiresOn, and set a secure, HttpOnly cookie NB_SID containing the raw session token (cookie is Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Expires matches session).
•	Server logs an authentication success event (no PIN/token).
•	On failure:
•	Increment FailedAttemptCount and set LockedUntil when threshold reached.
•	Return generic 401 Unauthorized with a generic error message — no user enumeration.
•	Server logs failure/lockout events without sensitive data.
Session flow
•	Server stores only hashed token in CustomerSessions.TokenHash.
•	Cookie NB_SID contains the raw token (HttpOnly, Secure) for authentication.
•	CurrentUserService reads NB_SID from request cookies, hashes it with SHA256, looks up CustomerSession by TokenHash, ensures RevokedOn == null and ExpiresOn not passed, and returns CustomerId.
•	Application services/controllers should obtain authenticated CustomerId via ICurrentUserService.GetCurrentCustomerIdAsync().
•	Logout endpoint reads NB_SID cookie, calls AuthService.LogoutAsync(token) which finds session by hashed token and sets RevokedOn = UtcNow, then clears cookie.
Cookie configuration
•	Cookie name: NB_SID
•	HttpOnly = true
•	Secure = true
•	SameSite = Strict
•	Expires = session expiry (UTC)
Lockout policy (development demo)
•	Failed attempts threshold: 5
•	Lockout duration: 15 minutes
•	On failed PIN verification, FailedAttemptCount increments; if >= threshold, LockedUntil set to UtcNow + lockout duration.
•	While LockedUntil > UtcNow, authentication attempts are rejected.
•	Successful authentication resets FailedAttemptCount = 0 and clears LockedUntil.
